# Private paper route

## 1. Scientific objective and author claim

The paper studies neutral dichloro(eta2-nitrato)bis(triphenylphosphine)iridium(III), IrCl2(eta2-O2NO)(PPh3)2. The authors use DFT geometry and harmonic frequencies to support the pseudo-octahedral, bidentate-nitrato structural assignment and nitrate IR-band assignment. They also propose oxygen/air-mediated conversion of an alkyl-nitrite adduct through a nitrosyl-like intermediate.

## 2. System and model boundary

The modeled species is C36H30Cl2IrNO3P2: one Ir(III), two chloride ligands, two monodentate PPh3 ligands, and one nitrate ligand bound through two nitrate oxygens. The computational species is an isolated neutral singlet molecule. The comparison boundary is molecular bond lengths and angles plus harmonic IR frequencies; crystal packing, solvent, counterions, and solid-state intensity effects are outside the model.

